{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/06 18:20 SAST
Version: 0.6
Description:
  One seed set, broken down by table.

  Generation has always recorded what it wrote into each table, and nothing has ever shown it. The
  set list could only offer two whole-set totals, so a set that came out smaller than requested gave
  no way to see which tables were short.

  Two figures per table, because they answer different questions. Written is what generation
  produced and never changes. Remaining is counted from the physical rows now, so it falls when a
  cleanup runs, when another set's cleanup takes dependent rows with it, or when a row is deleted by
  hand. The two agreeing is the ordinary case; the difference is the interesting one.

  Tables neither written to nor holding anything are left out rather than listed as zero, so the
  table shows the shape of this set instead of the shape of the catalogue.

  Core owns this markup. Themes style it through the ordinary platform card, table and button
  classes.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.

Changelog:
  2026/09/06 18:20 SAST
  - Created so a seed set in the history list can be opened for its per-table record breakdown.
#}
{% extends layout %}

{% block page_body %}
{% set ph_back_href = '/admin/seed' %}
{% set ph_back_label = 'Seed Database' %}
{% set ph_kicker = 'Platform administration' %}
{% set ph_title = seed_set.description ?: 'Seed set' %}
{% set ph_lead = seed_set.seed_token %}
{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}

<section class="container-fluid cl-container-wide py-5">

  <div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white p-4"><h2 class="h4 mb-0">Set summary</h2></div>
    <div class="card-body p-4">
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Requested</strong><div>{{ seed_set.requested_volume }}</div></div>
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Written</strong><div>{{ seed_totals.initial }}</div></div>
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Remaining</strong><div>{{ seed_totals.current }}</div></div>
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Generated in</strong><div>{{ seed_set.generation_seconds }}s</div></div>
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Created</strong><div>{{ seed_set.created_at }}</div></div>
        <div class="col-md-4"><strong>Cleaned up</strong><div>{{ seed_set.cleaned_at ?: 'No' }}</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header bg-white p-4">
      <h2 class="h4 mb-1">Records per table</h2>
      <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">What generation wrote, beside what physically remains. The two agree until something removes rows: a cleanup, a cascade from another set, or a deletion made by hand.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-0">
        <thead><tr><th style="width:58%">Table</th><th style="width:14%">Written</th><th style="width:14%">Remaining</th><th style="width:14%">Removed</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for seed_row in seed_breakdown %}
            <tr>
              <td class="mono small">{{ seed_row.table }}</td>
              <td>{{ seed_row.initial }}</td>
              <td>{{ seed_row.current }}</td>
              <td>{{ seed_row.removed ?: '—' }}</td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
        <tfoot><tr><th>Total</th><th>{{ seed_totals.initial }}</th><th>{{ seed_totals.current }}</th><th>{{ seed_totals.initial - seed_totals.current }}</th></tr></tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if can_manage_seed and not seed_set.cleaned_at %}
    <div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-4">
      <a class="btn btn-outline-danger" href="/admin/seed/{{ seed_set.seed_token }}/cleanup">Clean up this set</a>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

</section>
{% endblock %}
